-- The Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018 (S.I. 2018/506).
-- Baseline: the questions a company providing an AI model service would ask.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in the law of
-- any part of the United Kingdom has read this against the source, and the source is an
-- aid that was NOT checked against the official text (NOTES.md).
--
-- These are cyber-security regulations, NOT an AI law. The UK has no AI-specific
-- incident-reporting duty that this session could find (NOTES.md). Nothing here says an
-- AI service is within the Regulations: whether it is a "cloud computing service",
-- "online search engine" or "online marketplace" is the provider's to state (fork F1).
--
-- Seat: the provider (a company). Every input is a fact it can state. The rules are in
-- nis-regulations.l4; this module only asks the questions and builds the records.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nis-domain`
IMPORT `nis-regulations`

§ `Do the NIS Regulations apply to me?`

@ref regulation 1(2) and (3)(e); regulation 8
@export Do the UK Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018 apply to me, as an operator of an essential service (OES) or as a relevant digital service provider (RDSP)? These are cyber-security regulations, not an AI law; an AI service is within them only if it is one of the kinds of digital service regulation 1 names.
GIVEN `information society service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your service an information society service within point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive (EU) 2015/1535 (the Regulations borrow the term; this encoding does not define it)?
      `cloud computing service` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service a "cloud computing service" within regulation 1(2): "a digital service that enables access to a scalable and elastic pool of shareable computing resources"? The Regulations say nothing about AI models or APIs; answer yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `online search engine` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service an "online search engine" within regulation 1(2): it lets users search, in principle, all websites (or all in a language) on a query and returns links to information on the requested content? Answer yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `online marketplace` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service an "online marketplace" within regulation 1(2): it lets consumers or traders conclude online sales or service contracts with traders? Answer yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `provided in the UK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide the service in the United Kingdom?
      `head office in the UK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your head office in the United Kingdom?
      `UK representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you nominated a representative established in the United Kingdom to act for you under these Regulations?
      `micro or small enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC? (The Regulations borrow that definition; this encoding does not restate it.)
      `OES` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an operator of an essential service: deemed designated under regulation 8(1) (you meet a Schedule 2 threshold) or 8(2A), or designated by a competent authority under regulation 8(3)? Schedule 2's essential services are in electricity, oil, gas, air, water, rail and road transport, health care, drinking water and digital infrastructure (TLD name registries, DNS services, internet exchange points); none of them is an AI model service, so answer no unless you also provide one of those.
GIVETH A `do the Regulations apply to me`
`do the NIS Regulations apply to me` `information society service` `cloud computing service` `online search engine` `online marketplace` `provided in the UK` `head office in the UK` `UK representative` `micro or small enterprise` `OES` MEANS
    `whether the Regulations apply to me`
        (`the provider as it describes itself` WITH
            `my service is an information society service within Article 1(1)(b) of Directive 2015/1535` IS `information society service`
            `is my service a cloud computing service`                       IS `cloud computing service`
            `is my service an online search engine`                         IS `online search engine`
            `is my service an online marketplace`                           IS `online marketplace`
            `I provide the service in the United Kingdom`                   IS `provided in the UK`
            `my head office is in the United Kingdom`                       IS `head office in the UK`
            `I have nominated a representative established in the United Kingdom` IS `UK representative`
            `I am a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS `micro or small enterprise`
            `I am an OES, designated or deemed designated under regulation 8` IS `OES`)

§ `Must I nominate a UK representative? -- only if my head office is outside the UK`

@ref regulation 14A(1) and (2)
@export Must I nominate a representative in the United Kingdom under regulation 14A of the UK Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018? It applies to a digital service provider with its head office outside the UK that offers digital services in the UK and is not a micro or small enterprise. Until you nominate one, you are not an RDSP under regulation 1(3)(e). The time limit (three months) is not computed here.
GIVEN `information society service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your service an information society service within point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive (EU) 2015/1535?
      `cloud computing service` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service a "cloud computing service" within regulation 1(2) ("a digital service that enables access to a scalable and elastic pool of shareable computing resources")? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `online search engine` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service an "online search engine" within regulation 1(2)? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `online marketplace` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service an "online marketplace" within regulation 1(2)? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `offered in the UK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer the service within the United Kingdom?
      `head office in the UK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your head office in the United Kingdom?
      `micro or small enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC?
GIVETH A `must I nominate a UK representative`
`must I nominate a UK representative` `information society service` `cloud computing service` `online search engine` `online marketplace` `offered in the UK` `head office in the UK` `micro or small enterprise` MEANS
    `whether I must nominate a UK representative`
        (`the provider as it describes itself` WITH
            `my service is an information society service within Article 1(1)(b) of Directive 2015/1535` IS `information society service`
            `is my service a cloud computing service`                       IS `cloud computing service`
            `is my service an online search engine`                         IS `online search engine`
            `is my service an online marketplace`                           IS `online marketplace`
            `I provide the service in the United Kingdom`                   IS `offered in the UK`
            `my head office is in the United Kingdom`                       IS `head office in the UK`
            -- Not read by regulation 14A: the duty is the same whether or not one is nominated.
            `I have nominated a representative established in the United Kingdom` IS FALSE
            `I am a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS `micro or small enterprise`
            -- Not read by regulation 14A.
            `I am an OES, designated or deemed designated under regulation 8` IS FALSE)

§ `An incident has happened: must I notify, and whom?`

@ref regulations 11(1), 12(3), 12(4) and 12(9)
@export Must I notify this incident under the UK Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018? An OES notifies a NIS incident (significant impact on the continuity of its essential service); an RDSP notifies an incident with a substantial impact on the provision of its digital service, if it has the information to assess that.
GIVEN `information society service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your service an information society service within point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive (EU) 2015/1535?
      `cloud computing service` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service a "cloud computing service" within regulation 1(2) ("a digital service that enables access to a scalable and elastic pool of shareable computing resources")? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `online search engine` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service an "online search engine" within regulation 1(2)? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `online marketplace` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service an "online marketplace" within regulation 1(2)? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `provided in the UK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide the service in the United Kingdom?
      `head office in the UK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your head office in the United Kingdom?
      `UK representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you nominated a representative established in the United Kingdom?
      `micro or small enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC?
      `OES` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an operator of an essential service, designated or deemed designated under regulation 8? Schedule 2's essential services are in electricity, oil, gas, air, water, rail and road transport, health care, drinking water and digital infrastructure (TLD name registries, DNS services, internet exchange points); none of them is an AI model service, so answer no unless you also provide one of those.
      `actual adverse effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the event have an actual adverse effect on the security of network and information systems (regulation 1(2), "incident")? A risk or near miss with no actual adverse effect is not an incident.
      `substantial impact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having taken into account the number of users affected, the duration, the geographical area, the extent of disruption to the service and the impact on economic and societal activities (regulation 12(7)), did the incident have a substantial impact on the provision of a digital service you provide? The deposited aid text of EU Regulation 2018/151 explains these parameters (Article 3) and sets no numeric threshold (its Article 4 is shown omitted); the judgment is yours.
      `information to assess` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have access to information that enables you to assess whether the impact of the incident is substantial (regulation 12(4))?
      `significant impact on essential service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an OES: having regard to the number of users affected, the duration and the geographical area (regulation 11(2)), did the incident have a significant impact on the continuity of your essential service? Answer no if you are not an OES.
      `RDSP incident affecting me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an OES: did an incident affecting an RDSP you rely on have a significant impact on the continuity of your essential service (regulation 12(9))? Answer no if you are not an OES.
GIVETH A `must I notify`
`must I notify this incident` `information society service` `cloud computing service` `online search engine` `online marketplace` `provided in the UK` `head office in the UK` `UK representative` `micro or small enterprise` `OES` `actual adverse effect` `substantial impact` `information to assess` `significant impact on essential service` `RDSP incident affecting me` MEANS
    `whether I must notify`
        (`the provider as it describes itself` WITH
            `my service is an information society service within Article 1(1)(b) of Directive 2015/1535` IS `information society service`
            `is my service a cloud computing service`                       IS `cloud computing service`
            `is my service an online search engine`                         IS `online search engine`
            `is my service an online marketplace`                           IS `online marketplace`
            `I provide the service in the United Kingdom`                   IS `provided in the UK`
            `my head office is in the United Kingdom`                       IS `head office in the UK`
            `I have nominated a representative established in the United Kingdom` IS `UK representative`
            `I am a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS `micro or small enterprise`
            `I am an OES, designated or deemed designated under regulation 8` IS `OES`)
        (`the event as I know it` WITH
            `the event had an actual adverse effect on the security of network and information systems` IS `actual adverse effect`
            `the incident had a substantial impact on the provision of a digital service I provide` IS `substantial impact`
            `I have access to information that enables me to assess whether the impact is substantial` IS `information to assess`
            `the incident had a significant impact on the continuity of my essential service` IS `significant impact on essential service`
            `an incident affecting an RDSP I rely on had a significant impact on the continuity of my essential service` IS `RDSP incident affecting me`)

@ref regulation 3(1) and (2); regulations 11(1), 12(3) and 12(9)
@export Whom must I notify about this incident under the UK Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018? An RDSP notifies the Information Commission; an OES notifies the competent authority designated for its subsector in Schedule 1.
GIVEN `information society service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your service an information society service within point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive (EU) 2015/1535?
      `cloud computing service` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service a "cloud computing service" within regulation 1(2)? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `online search engine` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service an "online search engine" within regulation 1(2)? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `online marketplace` IS A `my answer to a classification` @desc Is your service an "online marketplace" within regulation 1(2)? Yes, no, or I cannot say.
      `provided in the UK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide the service in the United Kingdom?
      `head office in the UK` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your head office in the United Kingdom?
      `UK representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you nominated a representative established in the United Kingdom?
      `micro or small enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC?
      `OES` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an operator of an essential service, designated or deemed designated under regulation 8? Schedule 2's essential services are in electricity, oil, gas, air, water, rail and road transport, health care, drinking water and digital infrastructure (TLD name registries, DNS services, internet exchange points); none of them is an AI model service, so answer no unless you also provide one of those.
      `actual adverse effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the event have an actual adverse effect on the security of network and information systems?
      `substantial impact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the incident have a substantial impact on the provision of a digital service you provide (regulation 12(7))?
      `information to assess` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have access to information that enables you to assess whether the impact is substantial (regulation 12(4))?
      `significant impact on essential service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an OES: did the incident have a significant impact on the continuity of your essential service (regulation 11)? Answer no if you are not an OES.
      `RDSP incident affecting me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an OES: did an incident affecting an RDSP you rely on have a significant impact on the continuity of your essential service (regulation 12(9))? Answer no if you are not an OES.
GIVETH A `whom must I notify`
`whom must I notify about this incident` `information society service` `cloud computing service` `online search engine` `online marketplace` `provided in the UK` `head office in the UK` `UK representative` `micro or small enterprise` `OES` `actual adverse effect` `substantial impact` `information to assess` `significant impact on essential service` `RDSP incident affecting me` MEANS
    `whom I must notify`
        (`the provider as it describes itself` WITH
            `my service is an information society service within Article 1(1)(b) of Directive 2015/1535` IS `information society service`
            `is my service a cloud computing service`                       IS `cloud computing service`
            `is my service an online search engine`                         IS `online search engine`
            `is my service an online marketplace`                           IS `online marketplace`
            `I provide the service in the United Kingdom`                   IS `provided in the UK`
            `my head office is in the United Kingdom`                       IS `head office in the UK`
            `I have nominated a representative established in the United Kingdom` IS `UK representative`
            `I am a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS `micro or small enterprise`
            `I am an OES, designated or deemed designated under regulation 8` IS `OES`)
        (`the event as I know it` WITH
            `the event had an actual adverse effect on the security of network and information systems` IS `actual adverse effect`
            `the incident had a substantial impact on the provision of a digital service I provide` IS `substantial impact`
            `I have access to information that enables me to assess whether the impact is substantial` IS `information to assess`
            `the incident had a significant impact on the continuity of my essential service` IS `significant impact on essential service`
            `an incident affecting an RDSP I rely on had a significant impact on the continuity of my essential service` IS `RDSP incident affecting me`)

§ `By when must I notify?`

@ref regulations 11(3)(b)(i), 12(6)(a) and 12(9)
@export By when must I notify, under the UK Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018, if I became aware at a given date and time? Gives the outer limit: exactly 72 hours (not 3 business days) after the moment of awareness, for an OES's NIS incident (regulation 11) or an RDSP's incident (regulation 12(3)); none for regulation 12(9), which says only "without undue delay". "Without undue delay" may require notice sooner.
GIVEN `which duty` IS A `a notification duty` @desc Which duty are you notifying under: regulation 11(1) (an OES's NIS incident), regulation 12(3) (an RDSP's incident) or regulation 12(9) (an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on)?
      `aware on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the clock start (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-02)? For an RDSP: when you were first aware that an incident had occurred (regulation 12(6)(a)). For an OES: when you were aware that a NIS incident, one with a significant impact, had occurred (regulation 11(3)(b)(i)).
      `aware hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour (0 to 23) on that date? The Regulations name no time zone: use one clock for every time you give, e.g. UTC.
      `aware minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute (0 to 59) of that hour?
GIVETH A MAYBE `a moment`
`by when must I notify` `which duty` `aware on` `aware hour` `aware minute` MEANS
    `the last moment to notify under` `which duty`
        (`a moment` WITH
            `day`    IS `aware on`
            `hour`   IS `aware hour`
            `minute` IS `aware minute`)

@ref regulations 11(3)(b)(i), 12(6)(a) and 12(9)
@export Was my notification made within the 72-hour outer limit of the UK Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018? A notice exactly 72 hours after the moment of awareness is in time; one minute later is late. No answer for regulation 12(9), which sets no outer limit.
GIVEN `which duty` IS A `a notification duty` @desc Which duty: regulation 11(1) (an OES's NIS incident), regulation 12(3) (an RDSP's incident) or regulation 12(9) (an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on)?
      `aware on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the clock start (for an RDSP, when you were first aware that an incident had occurred; for an OES, when you were aware that a NIS incident had occurred)?
      `aware hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour (0 to 23)? Use one clock, e.g. UTC, for every time you give.
      `aware minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute (0 to 59)?
      `notified on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you notify?
      `notified hour` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour (0 to 23), on the same clock?
      `notified minute` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute (0 to 59)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`was my notification within 72 hours` `which duty` `aware on` `aware hour` `aware minute` `notified on` `notified hour` `notified minute` MEANS
    `the notice was within the outer limit under` `which duty`
        (`a moment` WITH
            `day`    IS `aware on`
            `hour`   IS `aware hour`
            `minute` IS `aware minute`)
        (`a moment` WITH
            `day`    IS `notified on`
            `hour`   IS `notified hour`
            `minute` IS `notified minute`)

§ `What can be done to me? -- only if I failed to notify`

@ref regulations 17(1)-(2) and 18(1), (2), (6), (7)
@export What is the most I can be penalised under the UK Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018 for failing to notify an incident? Gives the ceiling in regulation 18(6) (1,000,000, 8,500,000 or 17,000,000 pounds) and its conditions. Whether a penalty is imposed, and how much up to the ceiling, is for the authority.
GIVEN `which duty` IS A `a notification duty` @desc Which duty: regulation 11(1) (an OES's NIS incident), regulation 12(3) (an RDSP's incident) or regulation 12(9) (an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on)?
      `what happened` IS A `what happened to my notification` @desc What happened: I notified in time with the required information; I did not notify at all; I notified, but more than 72 hours after the clock started; I notified in time, but without the required information (an item of regulation 11(3)(a) for an OES, or of regulation 12(5) for an RDSP); or, for an RDSP, I notified in time with the regulation 12(5) items, but not enough for the Information Commission to determine the significance of any cross-border impact (regulation 12(6)(b)).
      `reading` IS A `a reading of late RDSP notice` @desc For an RDSP's late notice, or one short on cross-border information, only: regulation 17(2) lists failures under regulation 12(3) and 12(5) but not 12(6), where the 72 hours and the cross-border requirement are. Reading A treats a breach of 12(6) as a failure to notify under 12(3); reading B treats it as not listed. The text does not settle it; pick one to see its answer.
      `enforcement notice` IS A `the enforcement notice position` @desc Was an enforcement notice served on you for this failure, and if it required steps, did you take them within its period?
      `authority's view` IS A `the authority's view of the contravention` @desc Has the authority (your designated competent authority, or the Information Commission) determined whether the contravention has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, your service provision?
GIVETH A `the most I can be penalised`
`what is the most I can be penalised for failing to notify` `which duty` `what happened` `reading` `enforcement notice` `authority's view` MEANS
    `the penalty ceiling for my failure to notify` `which duty` `what happened` `reading` `enforcement notice` `authority's view`
